<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Carte românească de învățătură</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1646">1646</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Pravila lui Vasile Lupu</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Carte românească de învățătură ('Romanian book of instruction') is a law code issued in Iași in 1646 by Prince <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vasile-lupu">Vasile Lupu</a> of Moldavia. Drawing on Byzantine law, it was one of the first law codes printed in Romanian. It dealt with agrarian matters and criminal law and was printed at the Three Hierarchs Monastery.</p></div>
